From: Macron <macron@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 02:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Don't retain an OpenGL context that is being
 freed.

-[NSOpenGLContext dealloc] calls -clearDrawable. Off the main thread,
WineOpenGLContext's override sends [super clearDrawable] to the main
thread in a block, and copying the block retains self, the context
being freed. The main thread releases the block after it has woken the
waiting thread, so that release can reach the context after this
thread has freed it: objc_release on freed memory, on the main thread,
and the process dies with c0000005 "in system thread".

It happens when the last reference to a context goes away off the main
thread, for example in wglDeleteContext or thread cleanup when no
main-thread block still holds the context. wined3d does that while it
creates its adapter: a context on a hidden window, then deleted.

While deallocating, reach the main thread through a __block variable,
which a block does not retain under manual reference counting.
---
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
@@ -30,11 +30,15 @@
 
 
 @interface WineOpenGLContext ()
+{
+    BOOL deallocating;
+}
 @property (retain, nonatomic) NSView* latentView;
 @property (nullable, weak) NSView *view;    /* redeclare this to avoid NSOpenGLContext's deprecation warnings */
 
     + (NSView*) dummyView;
     - (void) wine_updateBackingSize:(const CGSize*)size;
+    - (void) wine_superClearDrawable;
 
 @end
 
@@ -45,6 +49,7 @@
 
     - (void) dealloc
     {
+        deallocating = TRUE;
         [[self view] release];
         [latentView release];
         [super dealloc];
@@ -146,11 +151,27 @@
         [oldView release];
     }
 
+    - (void) wine_superClearDrawable
+    {
+        [super clearDrawable];
+    }
+
     - (void) clearDrawable
     {
         NSView* oldView = [self view];
         if ([NSThread isMainThread])
             [super clearDrawable];
+        else if (deallocating)
+        {
+            /* -[NSOpenGLContext dealloc] calls this.  A block that captures
+               self would retain the context while it is being freed, and the
+               main thread would release it after this thread has freed it.
+               A __block variable is not retained. */
+            __block WineOpenGLContext* context = self;
+            OnMainThread(^{
+                [context wine_superClearDrawable];
+            });
+        }
         else OnMainThread(^{
             [super clearDrawable];
         });
